---
import Journey from '../../layouts/Journey.astro';
import Step from '../../components/journey/Step.astro';
import Next from '../../components/journey/Next.astro';
import More from '../../components/journey/More.astro';
import ForLevel from '../../components/level/ForLevel.astro';
import CopyPrompt from '../../components/site/CopyPrompt.astro';
import Fact from '../../components/data/Fact.astro';
import Verified from '../../components/data/Verified.astro';
import LessonRef from '../../components/journey/LessonRef.astro';
import Term from '../../components/journey/Term.astro';
---
<Journey chapter="check" first="done" title="Make it prove it" description="An agent says done whether or not the work is right. A check between the agent and you sends broken work back; each kind of check catches one kind of wrong.">
  <Step id="done" title="It says “done” either way">
    <p>The <Term id="agent" /> from <LessonRef id="loop" />, given six made-up jobs. Four come out broken, in orange, and all six arrive marked “done”.</p>
  </Step>

  <Step id="tests" title="Put a check in the way">
    <ForLevel is="plain">
      <p>The posts between the agent and you are the <Term id="check" />: before it says done, the agent runs the app and clicks through it. Broken work goes back to the agent instead of on to you.</p>
      <More title="A prompt for this">
        <CopyPrompt compact title="Ask it to check before it says done">{`Before you tell me it is done:\n1. Start the app and click through what you changed.\n2. Tell me what you clicked and what you saw.\n3. If anything is wrong, fix it first.`}</CopyPrompt>
      </More>
    </ForLevel>
    <ForLevel is="technical">
      <p>The posts between the agent and you are the <Term id="check" />: <code>tsc --noEmit &amp;&amp; npm test</code>, run by the agent before it reports. A red result goes back into its loop.</p>
      <More title="A prompt for this" level="technical">
        <CopyPrompt compact title="Done means green">{`Before reporting done:\n1. Run tsc --noEmit and npm test. Paste the last lines of each.\n2. Add a test that fails without your change.\n3. If the UI changed, run the browser check at 390 px and 1280 px.`}</CopyPrompt>
      </More>
    </ForLevel>
    <ForLevel is="engineer">
      <p>The posts between the agent and you are the <Term id="check" />, one command the agent must run green before it reports: types and unit tests first, because they are fast and give the same answer every time.</p>
      <More title="One command" level="engineer">
        <pre class="j-code"><code>{`// package.json
"scripts": {
  "check": "tsc --noEmit && vitest run",
  "check:all": "npm run check && playwright test"
}`}</code></pre>
        <p>Put <code>npm run check</code> in AGENTS.md as the definition of done.</p>
      </More>
    </ForLevel>
  </Step>

  <Step id="more" title="Each check catches one kind of wrong">
    <p>Switch one off and the six jobs run again. The kind of wrong it was catching now reaches you.</p>
    <ForLevel is="plain">
      <div class="pick" data-multi role="group" aria-label="Checks that are on">
        <button type="button" data-do="toggle" data-val="run" data-default aria-pressed="true">It runs the app</button>
        <button type="button" data-do="toggle" data-val="phone" data-default aria-pressed="true">It looks on a phone</button>
      </div>
    </ForLevel>
    <ForLevel is="technical engineer">
      <div class="pick" data-multi role="group" aria-label="Checks that are on">
        <button type="button" data-do="toggle" data-val="types" data-default aria-pressed="true">tsc --noEmit</button>
        <button type="button" data-do="toggle" data-val="tests" data-default aria-pressed="true">npm test</button>
        <button type="button" data-do="toggle" data-val="browser" data-default aria-pressed="true">Browser check</button>
      </div>
    </ForLevel>
    <More title="Where each check runs" level="engineer">
      <dl class="j-defs">
        <dt><code>tsc --noEmit</code></dt><dd>Seconds. In the agent’s loop and in a pre-commit hook. Catches broken contracts, not wrong values.</dd>
        <dt>Unit tests</dt><dd>Seconds to a minute. In the loop and in CI on every push. Catch wrong logic you wrote a test for.</dd>
        <dt>Browser check</dt><dd>Minutes. In CI before merge. Catches layout and wiring a unit test never renders.</dd>
      </dl>
    </More>
  </Step>

  <Step id="spec" title="No check sees what nobody wrote down">
    <p>Every check is on, and hidden ratings still reach you in the CSV. Turn your rule into a check and run again.</p>
    <div class="row">
      <button class="btn" type="button" data-do="spec" aria-pressed="false">Make the rule a check</button>
    </div>
    <More title="A prompt for this">
      <CopyPrompt compact title="Turn a rule into a test">{`Rule: a member who hides their rating must never have it shown or exported.\nWrite a test that fails if a hidden rating appears anywhere, including the CSV export.\nRun it before your fix and after, and show me both results.`}</CopyPrompt>
      <p><Fact id="harnesses.claudeCode.checkToRun" show="claim" /></p>
    </More>
    <Next from="check" more={[{ href: 'wiki/verification/', text: 'Verification', side: true }, { href: 'journey/proof/', text: 'Proof you can read, lesson 16' }]} />
  </Step>
  <Fragment slot="foot">
    <p>The six jobs, their bugs and the error messages are made up.</p>
    <Verified ids={['harnesses.claudeCode.checkToRun']} />
  </Fragment>
</Journey>
